flowchart LR
  accTitle: Mechanism-specific migration depth D0 to D4
  accDescr: Five thresholds describe the implementation depth of one mapped mechanism: conceptual resemblance, callable interface, explicit state and components, trigger-exercised runtime control, and outcome-adapted future control policy.
  D0["D0\nConceptual resemblance\nLabel or comparable idea"] --> D1["D1\nInterface correspondence\nCallable operation"]
  D1 --> D2["D2\nState/component structure\nMapped state is explicit"]
  D2 --> D3["D3\nRuntime control law\nTrigger executes transition"]
  D3 --> D4["D4\nAdaptive control law\nOutcome updates future policy"]
  NOTE["Applies to the mapped mechanism only — not a whole architecture or product"]
  D2 -.-> NOTE
  D3 -.-> NOTE
  D4 -.-> NOTE
  classDef base fill:#EAF4FB,stroke:#1A4A8A,color:#1C1C1E
  classDef runtime fill:#EEF7EE,stroke:#27AE60,color:#1C1C1E
  classDef adaptive fill:#F0F0FF,stroke:#5B4FBE,color:#1C1C1E
  classDef note fill:#FEF9E7,stroke:#F39C12,color:#1C1C1E
  class D0,D1,D2 base
  class D3 runtime
  class D4 adaptive
  class NOTE note
